# Documentation and diagram sync

When you add, remove, or change API or database behavior, update the matching documentation in the **same change**.

## API changes

Touch these files together:

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| New/changed route in `apps/api/src/modules/**` | `packages/openapi/spec/openapi.yaml` (path, method, params, schemas, security) |
| New/changed Zod schema in `@vaultstack/validation` used by an API | Matching `components/schemas` in `openapi.yaml` |
| Auth, CSRF, or org-context behavior | `openapi.yaml` security schemes + `docs/api/README.md` Authentication section |
| New error codes | `openapi.yaml` `ApiError` enum + `docs/api/README.md` error section |

After editing the spec, verify:

- `pnpm --filter @vaultstack/openapi test`
- Interactive docs still load at `http://localhost:3000/api/docs` when the API is running

## Database schema changes

When editing `packages/database/prisma/schema.prisma`:

1. Add or update the Prisma migration.
2. Update `docs/architecture/database-schema.md`:
   - Mermaid `erDiagram` entities and relationships
   - Domain groups table if a new model domain appears
   - Cascade notes if `onDelete` behavior changes

## Checklist before finishing

- [ ] OpenAPI paths match registered Express routes
- [ ] Markdown API reference (`docs/api/README.md`) matches OpenAPI where both exist
- [ ] ER diagram reflects every FK relation in `schema.prisma`
- [ ] New npm deps documented in `docs/development/dependencies.md`
